    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Continue weekly prolonged exposure; I expect about four more sessions to complete the course. [S]</item><item>Continue behavioral alcohol treatment and the veteran recovery peer group. Revisit naltrexone or acamprosate with Dr. Marquez if heavy-drinking days recur during the rest of therapy. [S]</item><item>Avoid benzodiazepines and sedative sleep medicines, which can undermine exposure therapy and add to the risk with alcohol. [S]</item><item>Plan for nights after hard sessions: a call to a peer, no alcohol in the house, and the wind-down routine from therapy. [S]</item><item>Repeat PCL-5, AUDIT-C, and PHQ-9 at twelve weeks. [S]</item><item>For sleep, keep a regular rise time and do not use alcohol as a sleep aid; if insomnia persists after the course, cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia. [S]</item><item>Keep the safety plan current, with the crisis line (988, press 1) in his phone. [S]</item><item>Report sent to Dr. Marquez and discussed with her the same day; he agrees with the plan. [S]</item><item>Follow-up: Weekly prolonged exposure through the end of the course, then a booster session on request. Behavioral health will see him sooner for a rise in PCL-5, a return to heavy drinking, or any suicidal thoughts. [S]</item></list></text>

